---
import BinarySearch from '../components/BinarySearch.astro';
import LabLayout from '../layouts/LabLayout.astro';

const lessonUrl = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/lessons/binary-search/`;
---
<LabLayout title="Binary Search Lab" description="An interactive lesson on binary search.">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">ALGORITHMS LAB</p>
    <h1>Binary search</h1>
    <p>Find a target in a sorted array. Before each step, predict which half the algorithm will keep.</p>
  </header>
  <BinarySearch />
  <p><a href={lessonUrl}>Read the binary search lesson</a></p>
  <section>
    <h2>Why it works</h2>
    <p>When the target is larger than the midpoint, every number to the left is too small. When it’s smaller, the numbers to the right are too large. Each comparison cuts the remaining search interval roughly in half, so the worst case grows as <code>O(log n)</code>.</p>
    <p>Try searching for <strong>24</strong> to see how the algorithm handles a missing value.</p>
  </section>
</LabLayout>
